    "body": "## Problem\n\nWith `outbuf=0`, switching buffers before an HTTP response arrives causes the response to overwrite the newly current buffer.\n\n## Solution\n\nCapture the concrete output buffer handle when starting the request. Cover a buffer switch before the response callback runs.",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-18T18:43:15Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42454#discussion_r4307648801"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/42454"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/4307648801"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "this test is kind of weak isn't it? the buffer might contain 'unrelated' but this wouldn't fail?",
            "commit_id": "d4f5a1045c650affa33befbbaa3c3fd81c9df2e9",
            "created_at": "2026-10-18T15:44:25Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -122,17 +122,24 @@ describe('vim.net.request', function()\n       local lines\n \n       local buf = vim.api.nvim_create_buf(false, true)\n+      vim.api.nvim_set_current_buf(buf)\n       ---@diagnostic disable-next-line: param-type-mismatch\n-      vim.net.request(url, { outbuf = buf })\n+      vim.net.request(url, { outbuf = 0 })\n+\n+      -- Switch buffers before the response arrives.\n+      local other = vim.api.nvim_create_buf(true, false)\n+      vim.api.nvim_set_current_buf(other)\n+      vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(other, 0, -1, true, { 'unrelated text' })\n \n       vim.wait(2000, function()\n         lines = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(buf, 0, -1, false)\n         return lines[1] ~= ''\n       end)\n \n-      return lines\n+      return { lines, vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(other, 0, -1, true) }\n     end)\n-    assert(content and content[1]:find('html'))\n+    assert(content[1] and content[1][1]:find('html'))",
